WEBVTT

00:01:30.370 --> 00:01:34.508
"Tenchi Muyo: Time and Space Adventures"

00:01:34.508 --> 00:01:35.375
"Tenchi Muyo: Time and Space Adventures"
Ladies and gentlemen!

00:01:35.375 --> 00:01:37.077
Ladies and gentlemen!

00:01:37.077 --> 00:01:42.749
Today, we are bringing you the conclusion
of Tenchi Muyo's special episodes.

00:01:42.749 --> 00:01:45.819
Because the dimension
tuner got out of control,

00:01:45.819 --> 00:01:52.359
our heroes have been
traveling through different worlds.

00:01:52.359 --> 00:01:55.529
How will this time and space travel end?

00:01:55.529 --> 00:02:01.695
Please find out with all of
your family where they are going!

00:02:13.046 --> 00:02:14.781
All right, I'm off.

00:02:14.781 --> 00:02:16.583
Wait, honey.

00:02:16.583 --> 00:02:18.084
Huh?

00:02:18.084 --> 00:02:21.281
Your tie isn't straight.

00:02:22.722 --> 00:02:25.859
There. That's much better.

00:02:25.859 --> 00:02:27.060
Bye.

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:29.551
See you in the evening!

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:38.538
Sasami, you'd better hurry up
or you'll be late for school.

00:02:38.538 --> 00:02:40.207
I'm coming!

00:02:40.207 --> 00:02:42.409
Do you have everything you need?

00:02:42.409 --> 00:02:46.780
Yup. Ah, Mom, please don't
forget to feed Ryo-Ohki, okay?

00:02:46.780 --> 00:02:49.149
Oh, no, I won't.

00:02:49.149 --> 00:02:50.350
I'd better get going.

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:53.353
Sasami, be careful of the traffic.

00:02:53.353 --> 00:02:55.048
All right!

00:03:00.961 --> 00:03:05.398
Huh? Oh, the old maid of the house.

00:03:05.398 --> 00:03:08.568
Are you calling me an old maid?

00:03:08.568 --> 00:03:12.405
Sorry. You are up early today, huh?

00:03:12.405 --> 00:03:16.977
Yeah, yeah. I am the nagging sister-in-law.

00:03:16.977 --> 00:03:19.646
I gripe about a lot of things,

00:03:19.646 --> 00:03:22.376
because I am responsible
for keeping this house running.

00:03:23.483 --> 00:03:25.318
Ugh! Too salty!

00:03:25.318 --> 00:03:29.089
What is the deal with this <i>miso</i> soup?

00:03:29.089 --> 00:03:30.490
I'm terribly sorry.

00:03:30.490 --> 00:03:32.225
If you were someone I could count on,

00:03:32.225 --> 00:03:36.763
I would not hesitate to get married and
leave this house in your care, you know.

00:03:36.763 --> 00:03:42.802
Look at you. You are just sitting
around and spacing out all day... Huh?

00:03:42.802 --> 00:03:45.505
What is this weird stuff?

00:03:45.505 --> 00:03:48.275
Well, it's a croquette, Sis.

00:03:48.275 --> 00:03:52.045
You call this charcoal a croquette?

00:03:52.045 --> 00:03:54.047
Sorry about that.

00:03:54.047 --> 00:04:00.350
Hmph... you just cannot get
anything straight, can you?

00:04:06.259 --> 00:04:07.494
Could you move a little slower?

00:04:07.494 --> 00:04:10.363
You do not have to take
all day on this, you know.

00:04:10.363 --> 00:04:12.763
Sorry.

00:04:15.435 --> 00:04:17.404
Here. Look at this!

00:04:17.404 --> 00:04:19.673
These screens are accumulating dust.

00:04:19.673 --> 00:04:21.374
I'll get it.

00:04:21.374 --> 00:04:23.343
This area is pretty dirty, too.

00:04:23.343 --> 00:04:25.412
I'm wiping there right now.

00:04:25.412 --> 00:04:26.479
Do not forget this part.

00:04:26.479 --> 00:04:28.811
R-Right away, Sis!

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:35.088
Oh, my. Did you notice this mess here?

00:04:35.088 --> 00:04:36.715
I'm coming!

00:04:45.966 --> 00:04:48.168
There.

00:04:48.168 --> 00:04:51.972
When did you do laundry last?

00:04:51.972 --> 00:04:55.567
I have told you many times that you
should do laundry more often, haven't I?

00:04:57.811 --> 00:05:00.814
L-I'm sorry.

00:05:00.814 --> 00:05:02.849
Uh, not so much, Mihoshi!

00:05:02.849 --> 00:05:06.553
You must not waste detergent like that.

00:05:06.553 --> 00:05:10.490
I'll be more careful.

00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:13.026
Are you sure about this, Sis?

00:05:13.026 --> 00:05:16.162
Today is not our trash day.

00:05:16.162 --> 00:05:18.865
It is all right as long
as we do not get caught.

00:05:18.865 --> 00:05:20.730
Eat well.

00:05:24.537 --> 00:05:28.908
You have a strange name for a cat, Ryo-Ohki.

00:05:28.908 --> 00:05:33.470
Whiskers is more like a
normal cat's name, don't you think?

00:05:34.681 --> 00:05:35.515
Huh?

00:05:35.515 --> 00:05:39.386
Mihoshi! This says
that meat is half off today!

00:05:39.386 --> 00:05:41.154
Huh?

00:05:41.154 --> 00:05:43.588
It says it right here.

00:05:47.427 --> 00:05:49.029
Excuse me!

00:05:49.029 --> 00:05:54.300
Five hundred grams of
roast beef... I mean pork!

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:59.237
And 300 grams of diced meat, please.

00:06:00.340 --> 00:06:03.776
Ahh, I feel exhausted.

00:06:05.512 --> 00:06:07.013
Huh?

00:06:07.013 --> 00:06:10.813
Since I'm already in the neighborhood...

00:06:17.323 --> 00:06:20.627
Kiyone, you have a call on line one.

00:06:20.627 --> 00:06:22.117
Thank you.

00:06:23.797 --> 00:06:26.866
Hello, this is Kiyone.

00:06:26.866 --> 00:06:28.935
Ugh!

00:06:28.935 --> 00:06:30.570
You know what?

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:35.375
My husband's sister is such a nit-picker.

00:06:35.375 --> 00:06:39.279
She is always finding fault
and yelling at me all day long.

00:06:39.279 --> 00:06:42.582
When I say, "What's wrong?"
She says stuff like,

00:06:42.582 --> 00:06:49.389
"What was that croquette
you served this morning?"

00:06:49.389 --> 00:06:52.425
Hey! If all you wanted
to do was complain,

00:06:52.425 --> 00:06:54.928
I've got lots of work to do, you know.

00:06:54.928 --> 00:06:59.132
But it's not like we get to
see each other that often.

00:06:59.132 --> 00:07:01.935
We've been getting together
quite frequently since our graduation.

00:07:01.935 --> 00:07:03.036
Really?

00:07:03.036 --> 00:07:08.975
Uh-huh! Besides, you always tell me
the same old story every time I see you!

00:07:08.975 --> 00:07:11.211
Frustration is not good for you.

00:07:11.211 --> 00:07:13.546
Why don't you get
married or something, Kiyone?

00:07:13.546 --> 00:07:14.814
That's none of your business.

00:07:14.814 --> 00:07:15.982
Excuse me.

00:07:15.982 --> 00:07:19.018
I'd like to have another
chocolate parfait, please.

00:07:19.018 --> 00:07:20.920
Are you listening to me?

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:22.756
Of course I am.

00:07:22.756 --> 00:07:26.159
Going back to my sister-in-law,

00:07:26.159 --> 00:07:31.231
she calls me slow and dumb
and all kinds of names, you know.

00:07:31.231 --> 00:07:33.333
Excuse me. I need a strawberry sundae here.

00:07:33.333 --> 00:07:34.994
Make it a large.

00:07:40.240 --> 00:07:43.107
I'm home.

00:07:53.019 --> 00:07:54.554
Hi, Mihoshi.

00:07:54.554 --> 00:07:58.158
Ah, Ryoko.

00:07:58.158 --> 00:08:00.026
We are out of soy sauce.

00:08:00.026 --> 00:08:02.262
Can you spare us some?

00:08:02.262 --> 00:08:07.033
- Sure. Just a minute... Huh?!
- Sorry to bother you like this all the time.

00:08:07.033 --> 00:08:08.301
- Ah, excuse me!
- Sorry to bother you like this all the time.

00:08:08.301 --> 00:08:10.937
I didn't invite you in, did I?

00:08:10.937 --> 00:08:13.072
Oh, don't mind me. Go on.

00:08:13.072 --> 00:08:16.276
You may be able to say that, but...

00:08:16.276 --> 00:08:19.679
Your husband hasn't come home yet, huh?

00:08:19.679 --> 00:08:21.848
Uh, Ryoko?

00:08:21.848 --> 00:08:25.251
Ahh, it's been a long day.

00:08:25.251 --> 00:08:27.887
Hi, Tenchi!

00:08:27.887 --> 00:08:29.856
Ahh! Oh, Ryoko!

00:08:29.856 --> 00:08:32.552
Welcome home.

00:08:33.359 --> 00:08:35.662
You know what? In Atami...

00:08:35.662 --> 00:08:37.430
Huh? What about Atami?

00:08:37.430 --> 00:08:40.166
My friend runs a bed
and breakfast place there.

00:08:40.166 --> 00:08:44.504
Don't you want to go with me?

00:08:44.504 --> 00:08:49.642
Don't seduce my husband!

00:08:49.642 --> 00:08:52.779
Uh, Ryoko, you are here again.

00:08:52.779 --> 00:08:54.781
Here comes the old bag.

00:08:54.781 --> 00:08:56.549
Who are you calling an old bag?!

00:08:56.549 --> 00:08:58.651
Ryoko, you are a widow, right?

00:08:58.651 --> 00:09:01.654
Can't you behave like one sometimes?

00:09:01.654 --> 00:09:04.524
It is very unpleasant to
see you flirting like that.

00:09:04.524 --> 00:09:09.359
Hmph. An old bag who's never
been married is far more unpleasant.

00:09:10.730 --> 00:09:12.527
You certainly have an attitude problem.

00:09:13.766 --> 00:09:16.569
Ayeka, Ryoko, stop that!

00:09:16.569 --> 00:09:19.739
The whole neighborhood can hear you.

00:09:19.739 --> 00:09:24.510
Tenchi, Atami is the place to go
when we run away to get married.

00:09:24.510 --> 00:09:26.312
Uh... hey, Ryoko!

00:09:26.312 --> 00:09:27.714
Come on, let's go.

00:09:27.714 --> 00:09:30.783
I'm sure everyone will give us their blessing.

00:09:30.783 --> 00:09:33.377
- We certainly won't!
- We certainly won't!

00:10:12.292 --> 00:10:14.351
Ya-hoo!

00:10:18.264 --> 00:10:21.200
We've done it!

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:23.536
There's nothing like robbing a bank, huh?

00:10:23.536 --> 00:10:28.007
Why am I even doing this sort of thing?

00:10:28.007 --> 00:10:30.510
The point is that we
are having fun together.

00:10:30.510 --> 00:10:32.779
I don't find this amusing at all!

00:10:32.779 --> 00:10:35.111
I do!

00:10:59.305 --> 00:11:03.176
Ryoko, the gangster that has been
terrorizing the whole United States

00:11:03.176 --> 00:11:09.082
is still at large despite a
nationwide manhunt by the police.

00:11:09.082 --> 00:11:11.351
It's been a month since Tenchi Motherskey,

00:11:11.351 --> 00:11:13.853
who is the grandson of the
Reverend Motherskey at St. Masaki,

00:11:13.853 --> 00:11:18.591
was kidnapped by Ryoko. His
well-being has been our major concern.

00:11:18.591 --> 00:11:23.162
He is now a wanted man, suspected
of being Ryoko's confederate,

00:11:23.162 --> 00:11:26.859
in the shooting at the Bronx Central Bank.

00:11:29.168 --> 00:11:33.373
FBI officers Mihoshi Grammy
and Kiyone McKinby declared

00:11:33.373 --> 00:11:36.399
that Ryoko's arrest is imminent.

00:11:38.144 --> 00:11:40.513
Jurai Financial Group's Miss Ayeka Jurai,

00:11:40.513 --> 00:11:43.683
who is Tenchi Motherskey's fiancée,
severely criticized the incompetence of FBI.

00:11:43.683 --> 00:11:47.720
She also announced that she
will offer a $1 million reward

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:51.986
for anyone with information that
leads to the arrest of the suspect.

00:11:54.794 --> 00:11:58.164
You should have consulted
with us before you offered a reward.

00:11:58.164 --> 00:12:03.202
People may think we are
incompetent or something.

00:12:03.202 --> 00:12:07.373
There is no doubt about it.
That is what you are!

00:12:07.373 --> 00:12:10.410
I cannot keep you in charge
of the investigation any longer.

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:14.647
Wait a minute. What are
you doing with that weapon?

00:12:14.647 --> 00:12:18.845
What else? I am going to
take care of Ryoko myself.

00:12:22.155 --> 00:12:23.756
You should be careful with that thing.

00:12:23.756 --> 00:12:26.859
Ayeka, please calm down.

00:12:26.859 --> 00:12:28.694
Let me go!

00:12:28.694 --> 00:12:32.598
While we are wasting time like this,
Ryoko and Tenchi are doing stuff like...

00:12:32.598 --> 00:12:35.735
I cannot allow it to go on any longer!

00:12:35.735 --> 00:12:39.466
- Oh, don't. Chill out!
- Get your hands off me!

00:12:45.945 --> 00:12:47.776
This way, Tenchi.

00:12:51.217 --> 00:12:54.209
Please cooperate. Thank you.

00:13:22.381 --> 00:13:24.611
Tenchi...

00:13:51.210 --> 00:13:56.282
Look, Tenchi. The Seto Bridge
is something else, isn't it?

00:13:56.282 --> 00:14:00.953
Ryoko, that's the Golden Gate Bridge.

00:14:00.953 --> 00:14:03.683
It doesn't matter either way.

00:14:04.924 --> 00:14:07.827
We can sure see a sky full of stars, huh?

00:14:07.827 --> 00:14:12.532
The stars are beautiful... don't you think?

00:14:12.532 --> 00:14:14.557
Ah, I guess.

00:14:15.935 --> 00:14:19.605
You and me... all alone under the starry sky.

00:14:19.605 --> 00:14:22.005
I don't know how I got myself into this mess.

00:14:23.843 --> 00:14:25.711
What is it?

00:14:25.711 --> 00:14:28.147
Oh, nothing. It's just that...

00:14:28.147 --> 00:14:31.284
It's just what?

00:14:31.284 --> 00:14:32.485
Hey, Tenchi.

00:14:32.485 --> 00:14:33.486
Huh?

00:14:33.486 --> 00:14:36.622
We've gone through a lot of stuff
since we started this journey, haven't we?

00:14:36.622 --> 00:14:38.758
We sure have.

00:14:38.758 --> 00:14:43.024
Ah, I just love stars.

00:15:02.248 --> 00:15:05.318
Washu! Is that really you?

00:15:05.318 --> 00:15:07.420
Long time no see.

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:09.889
So you've finally fixed that machine?

00:15:09.889 --> 00:15:11.891
It hasn't been easy.

00:15:11.891 --> 00:15:15.895
I had to eliminate the numerous different
worlds in order to catch up with you.

00:15:15.895 --> 00:15:20.066
All right. So now we can go
back to our original world, right?

00:15:20.066 --> 00:15:22.001
There is still one problem, though.

00:15:22.001 --> 00:15:23.302
What is it?

00:15:23.302 --> 00:15:28.040
You were the first one that tampered
with the machine, weren't you, Ryoko?

00:15:28.040 --> 00:15:30.009
Ah, I don't remember.

00:15:30.009 --> 00:15:35.514
The world seems to be reflecting
your idea of a perfect world.

00:15:35.514 --> 00:15:39.285
Oh! No wonder it's so messed up!

00:15:39.285 --> 00:15:43.756
I can't eliminate the world alone.

00:15:43.756 --> 00:15:49.092
Ryoko needs to renounce this world in
order for us to get back to our original one.

00:15:52.465 --> 00:15:53.899
No way!

00:15:53.899 --> 00:15:55.234
What?

00:15:55.234 --> 00:15:57.303
I will not deny this world, never!

00:15:57.303 --> 00:16:01.507
But don't you miss the original world, Ryoko?

00:16:01.507 --> 00:16:03.943
Nope. Not at all.

00:16:03.943 --> 00:16:07.480
Ryoko, you shouldn't be
so selfish at a time like this.

00:16:07.480 --> 00:16:10.249
Why don't you want to go back?

00:16:10.249 --> 00:16:14.287
Why?! Tenchi, haven't
we had some fun together?

00:16:14.287 --> 00:16:17.123
I just didn't have any other choices.

00:16:17.123 --> 00:16:21.227
I thought that... this world
was growing on you, Tenchi.

00:16:21.227 --> 00:16:23.496
That was wishful thinking on your part.

00:16:23.496 --> 00:16:25.931
Yeah, I was being hopeful.

00:16:25.931 --> 00:16:30.069
I believed we had this deep
bond between us. Didn't we?

00:16:30.069 --> 00:16:37.343
Do you hate the idea of
continuing to travel with me so much?

00:16:37.343 --> 00:16:39.834
Well, I'm just...

00:16:45.418 --> 00:16:47.477
I'm staying in this world!

00:16:48.921 --> 00:16:52.948
This is the world I desired. This is my world.

00:18:14.206 --> 00:18:16.175
Ryoko!

00:18:16.175 --> 00:18:19.779
Okay, let's go.

00:18:19.779 --> 00:18:21.514
Where are we going?

00:18:21.514 --> 00:18:23.983
We are going back to the
original world, aren't we?

00:18:23.983 --> 00:18:25.551
Uh, you feel okay about that?

00:18:25.551 --> 00:18:26.619
Yup.

00:18:26.619 --> 00:18:30.089
But you were so attached to this world.

00:18:30.089 --> 00:18:33.959
I realize this isn't a real journey.

00:18:33.959 --> 00:18:35.449
Ryoko.

00:18:36.395 --> 00:18:40.525
Now, Washu. I'm ready whenever
you are. Let's just get it over with.

00:18:41.667 --> 00:18:43.066
Okay.

00:18:50.409 --> 00:18:52.434
Ryoko's brain waves, check.

00:18:59.452 --> 00:19:01.352
The dimension tuner is now set.

00:19:05.224 --> 00:19:07.158
Now hang on!

00:19:19.672 --> 00:19:22.942
Ryoko... I... am...

00:19:22.942 --> 00:19:25.511
Don't say anything now, Tenchi.

00:19:25.511 --> 00:19:28.714
Otherwise, we'll never make it back.

00:19:28.714 --> 00:19:30.115
Ryoko!

00:19:30.115 --> 00:19:37.857
But someday, Tenchi, I will take
you on a real journey with me.

00:19:37.857 --> 00:19:40.121
I will... someday...

00:19:46.866 --> 00:19:50.169
Ahh, it's been very tiring, hasn't it?

00:19:50.169 --> 00:19:53.506
It has. We have been to Kyoto
and a northern fishing village and...

00:19:53.506 --> 00:19:55.474
It was very confusing.

00:19:55.474 --> 00:19:56.575
You didn't like it?

00:19:56.575 --> 00:19:58.873
I thought it was kind of fun.

00:19:59.745 --> 00:20:01.280
I had fun, too.

00:20:01.280 --> 00:20:03.883
You two are carefree.

00:20:03.883 --> 00:20:08.087
All this was caused by Ryoko.

00:20:08.087 --> 00:20:11.891
Huh?! Ryoko! Where is she?

00:20:11.891 --> 00:20:13.592
She is not around, huh?

00:20:13.592 --> 00:20:17.696
She must be flirting with Tenchi or something.

00:20:17.696 --> 00:20:20.165
Arrgg! I cannot stand the thought!

00:20:20.165 --> 00:20:23.569
Calm down, old maid.

00:20:23.569 --> 00:20:25.696
What did you call me?!

00:20:32.211 --> 00:20:33.701
Hey, Ryoko!

00:22:54.086 --> 00:22:56.855
A Juraian battleship
arrives on Earth without warning.

00:22:56.855 --> 00:22:59.725
They have come to arrest Ayeka!

00:22:59.725 --> 00:23:00.793
That's ridiculous!

00:23:00.793 --> 00:23:02.561
There must have been
some misunderstanding!

00:23:02.561 --> 00:23:05.798
Oh, well. You can't get away from the
consequences of your behavior, you see.

00:23:05.798 --> 00:23:08.200
But then they arrest Tenchi, too.

00:23:08.200 --> 00:23:09.068
What?!

00:23:09.068 --> 00:23:11.870
That was the beginning of the big
incident that rocks the entire universe.

00:23:11.870 --> 00:23:14.339
What has happened on Planet Jurai?

00:23:14.339 --> 00:23:16.208
Next episode is: "No Need for a Rebellion!"

00:23:16.208 --> 00:23:18.911
The shocking start of our space series!

00:23:18.911 --> 00:23:21.744
It's unquestionably a new development!
